{TEXT("将在「%s」配属本连；既有操练随队生效。"),TEXT("Assigned to the company at %s. Previous training remains in effect.")},
{TEXT("该编制暂未配属。 "),TEXT("This formation has not yet been assigned. ")},
{TEXT("新式冲锋枪留待春季攻势配发；既有训练仍然保留。 "),TEXT("The new submachine guns await the spring offensive. Previous training is retained. ")},
{TEXT("配属与地形"),TEXT("Attachments and terrain")},
{TEXT("配属与地形"),TEXT("Attachments and terrain"),TEXT("出发前的配属与地形")},
{TEXT("配属与地形"),TEXT("Attachments and terrain"),TEXT("Attachments and ground conditions")},
{TEXT("剪钳、探针和标记带不是普通步枪班的行头。工兵沿通路检查可疑引线与遗留弹药，剪开铁丝；他们需要时间，也需要身旁的掩护。"),TEXT("Wire cutters, probes and marking tape are not a rifleman's usual kit. Pioneers inspect suspect wires and abandoned ammunition, then cut a passage. They need time, and someone covering their work.")},
{TEXT("工兵先到障碍旁，步枪和机枪留出掩护火线。编制超过前线岗位后，在作战室选择本次出发的五种分队。"),TEXT("Send pioneers to the obstacle while rifles and machine guns cover them. Once more formations become available than the front can accommodate, choose five sections in the operations room.")},
{TEXT("Wex 喷火器适合贴近掩体后的短促喷射。沉重储罐、软管与有限的燃料，都意味着操作者无法像步枪手一样独自穿过无人区。"),TEXT("The Wex delivers short bursts against nearby cover. Its heavy tank, hose and limited fuel leave the operator dependent on an escort across no man's land.")},
{TEXT("法军 Schilt 分遣队受命参加本作的局部协同任务。他们穿自己的军服，背负储罐，以近处喷流清理掩体；这不是为英军常规步兵凭空配发的新枪。"),TEXT("A French Schilt detachment joins selected combined operations in this campaign. In French uniform, carrying its own tanks, it clears close cover with flame. It is an attached specialist formation, not standard British infantry equipment.")},
{TEXT("先用烟幕与机枪掩护接近，喷火手才有机会发挥作用。燃料有限，不能把火焰当作远程机枪。"),TEXT("Smoke and machine guns must cover the approach before flame can reach the position. Fuel is limited; this is a close assault weapon.")},
{TEXT("铁轨限定了它的战场"),TEXT("Its battlefield ends where the rails end")},
{TEXT("装甲列车只属于这条架空的铁路支线。炮车与机枪能掩护轨道旁的地段，断开的通路却会让钢铁失去机动；步兵仍必须争夺切口与观察位置。"),TEXT("The armoured train serves this fictional railway branch. Its guns cover the trackside, but broken rails can strand its armour. Infantry must still fight for the cutting and the observation posts.")},
{TEXT("守住铁路支点，让工兵先清理接近线，避免敌方反装甲炮获得从容射击的机会。"),TEXT("Secure the railway strongpoint. Let pioneers clear the approach and deny enemy anti-armour guns an undisturbed firing position.")},
{TEXT("反装甲火力盯住炮车，烟幕覆盖铁路旁的开阔地。让工兵与步枪分队交替接近中央切口。"),TEXT("Keep anti-armour guns on the gun wagon and smoke across the open trackside. Pioneers and rifle sections should approach the central cutting in turns.")},
{TEXT("带着还能归队的人"),TEXT("Bring back those who can still answer the roll")},
{TEXT("停战的消息还没有送到西线每一条战壕。村庄里仍有平民，通路里仍有障碍；本次不批准毒气和空中轰炸，新的配属要围绕地面掩护安排。"),TEXT("News of the armistice has not reached every trench. Civilians remain in the villages and obstacles block the routes. Gas and aerial bombing are not authorised here; prepare your attachments around ground support.")},
{TEXT("出发前查看受限的支援项目，保留工兵和能够相互掩护的小队。结束战斗以后，给战场上的人留下收尾的时间。"),TEXT("Check restricted support before departure. Keep pioneers and mutually supporting sections in the line. When the fighting ends, let the men on the field finish their part.")},
{TEXT("出发前的叮嘱"),TEXT("Before you go")},
{TEXT("本连配属命令"),TEXT("Company attachment orders")},
{TEXT("让每支小队有自己的任务"),TEXT("Give every section a task")},
{TEXT("后沿的电话时断时续。让机枪守住出口，步枪班接替空壕，突击队留作近处反击。没有一支小队能独自堵住整条战线。"),TEXT("The rear telephone line comes and goes. Machine guns cover the exits, rifle sections relieve empty trenches, and bombers wait for a close counterattack. No single section can seal the whole front.")},
{TEXT("走过阿拉斯与佛兰德，连队已经懂得分工：步枪占壕，刘易斯压住枪口，投弹手在掩护下接近。亚眠的晨雾里，这些本领必须一起用上。"),TEXT("After Arras and Flanders, the company knows its trades: rifles take trenches, Lewis guns suppress loopholes, and bombers close under cover. In the morning mist at Amiens, all three must work together.")},
{TEXT("分批推进，留一队预备。炮击还没停止时，不要把自己人送进弹着区。"),TEXT("Advance in bounds and keep a reserve. Do not send your own men into a barrage that has not lifted.")},
{TEXT("MP 18 风暴突击队"),TEXT("MP 18 stormtroopers")},
{TEXT("春季攻势的突击准备"),TEXT("Preparing the spring assault")},
{TEXT("风暴战术并非从这支新枪才开始。投弹手早已学会绕过强点、贴近壕口；如今新式冲锋枪能在近处送出短促火力，跟进步兵仍要负责守住通路。"),TEXT("Storm tactics preceded this new gun. Bombers already knew how to bypass strongpoints and close on a trench mouth. Submachine guns now add short bursts at close quarters; following infantry must still secure the route.")},
{TEXT("借雾接近，短点射压住壕口；把弹鼓留给近在眼前的突破口。"),TEXT("Approach through the mist and pin the trench mouth with short bursts. Save the drum for the breach immediately ahead.")},
{TEXT("本连尚未完成冲锋枪训练。先用现有投弹班作战，战后在作战室安排风暴队操练。"),TEXT("The company has not completed submachine-gun training. Fight with the existing bombing section, then arrange stormtrooper instruction in the operations room.")},
{TEXT("步枪班先到。用壕肩稳住枪托，辨清目标再开火；越过无人区之前，先给身后的同伴留出能掩护你的枪位。"),TEXT("The rifle section arrives first. Rest the stock against the trench shoulder and identify the target before firing. Before crossing no man's land, leave your comrades a position from which they can cover you.")},
{TEXT("点击壕旁的小队肖像出击。前壕满员时，增援会继续寻找前方的落脚处。"),TEXT("Select a section portrait beside the trench to advance. If the next trench is full, reinforcements continue looking for a position farther forward.")},
{TEXT("步枪班旁多了携带柄式手榴弹的突击手。他们不是隔着无人区投弹的神射手；真正的机会来自烟幕、坑岸，以及被友军压住的壕口。"),TEXT("Bombers carrying stick grenades now accompany the rifles. They cannot throw unerringly across no man's land: their chance comes from smoke, crater lips and a trench mouth suppressed by comrades.")},
{TEXT("投弹手带着 Mills 手榴弹来到本连。壕道的转角遮住步枪火线，手雷便有了用处；但雨水、紧张与奔跑都会让落点偏离预想。"),TEXT("The company receives Mills bombs. A turn in the trench can conceal an enemy from rifle fire and make the grenade indispensable. Rain, fear and a running throw can all send it astray.")},
{TEXT("先压制，再接近。不要把投弹班单独送进机枪射界；贴得太近，手雷也会伤到自己人。"),TEXT("Suppress first, then close. Never send bombers alone into a machine gun's field of fire. At very close range, their grenades can kill comrades too.")},
{TEXT("MG 08/15 组已配属。枪手负责火线，弹药手守住身侧；沉重的装备不适合追逐每一个目标，把它放在能看住通路的阵位。"),TEXT("An MG 08/15 section is attached. The gunner controls the lane while his ammunition bearer guards the flank. Heavy equipment cannot chase every target; place it where the route is in view.")},
{TEXT("刘易斯组终于跟上了本连。枪手用短促火力为步枪班争取抬头的机会，弹药手留在身边照应。机枪早已在战场上，这一次轮到你安排它的枪位。"),TEXT("The Lewis section has caught up with the company. Short bursts give the riflemen a chance to raise their heads, while the ammunition bearer stays close. Machine guns already rule this battlefield; now you must choose where yours will speak.")},
{TEXT("机枪留壕掩护，步枪分队推进。点射间隙与换弹都是真实的空当，别让枪位独自承受反击。"),TEXT("Leave machine guns covering from the trench while rifles advance. Bursts and reloads leave real gaps. Do not leave a gun position to face a counterattack alone.")},
{TEXT("精确射手会耐心寻找露出的枪手与观察位置。泥泞中的远处人影并不总是好目标；守住视线，才能让慢而稳的一枪值得等待。"),TEXT("Marksmen patiently seek exposed gunners and observation posts. A distant shape in the mud is not always a useful target. A clear line of sight makes a slow, deliberate shot worth the wait.")},
{TEXT("精确射手加入连队，专门留意敌人的机枪。军士提醒他：先看清，再扣扳机；镜瞄装备仍要经过作战室的专门操练。"),TEXT("Marksmen join the company to watch the enemy's guns. The sergeant insists: identify first, fire second. Telescopic sights still require specialist training in the operations room.")},
{TEXT("让射手停在有遮蔽的观察位置。烟幕会同时挡住双方；不要指望隔着浓烟辨认枪手。"),TEXT("Keep marksmen at sheltered observation positions. Smoke blinds both armies; do not expect them to identify a gunner through a dense screen.")},
{TEXT("指挥组赶到后，零散的枪位重新有了联络。士官把被压住的人喊回岗位；经任命的军官能伴随推进下令，身边的步枪手仍要负责掩护。"),TEXT("The command section restores contact between scattered gun positions. NCOs call pinned men back to their posts. Commissioned officers can give orders on the move, but nearby riflemen must still protect them.")},
{TEXT("军士带着指挥组来到前沿。他的口令能让被火力压住的人重新行动；经过任命后，军官以手枪自卫，把更多注意力留给观察与指挥。"),TEXT("The sergeant brings his command section forward. His orders can get suppressed men moving again. Once commissioned, an officer carries a pistol for protection and gives more attention to observation and command.")},
{TEXT("指挥组提高附近友军的命中率，并缓解压制。组长需要掩护。"),TEXT("Command sections improve nearby aim and relieve suppression. Protect the leader."),TEXT("指挥组靠近需要帮助的部队，别让组长第一个冲出壕口。命令能缓解压制，不能救回阵亡者。")},
{TEXT(" 秒"),TEXT(" seconds")},
{TEXT("此分队不存在。"),TEXT("This section does not exist.")},
