{TEXT("山脊下面的寂静"),TEXT("Silence beneath the ridge")},
{TEXT("澳新部队的测绘本"),TEXT("An ANZAC survey notebook")},
{TEXT("梅西讷山脊的地下传来过可疑声音，各支点仍奉命坚守。电话与备用枪位分开安置，以免一次爆炸切断整壕联络。"),TEXT("Suspicious sounds have been heard beneath Messines Ridge. The strongpoints are still ordered to hold. Keep the telephone separate from reserve gun positions so one blast cannot sever the trench's communications.")},
{TEXT("梅西讷山脊的地下传来过可疑声音，各支点仍奉命坚守。电话与备用枪位分开安置，以免一次爆炸切断整壕联络。"),TEXT("Suspicious sounds have been heard beneath Messines Ridge. The strongpoints are still ordered to hold. Keep the telephone separate from reserve gun positions so one blast cannot sever the trench's communications."),TEXT("梅西讷山脊的地下传来过可疑声音，眼下各支点收到的命令却仍是坚守。把电话与备用枪位分开安置，不能让一次爆炸带走整壕的联络。")},
{TEXT("梅西讷山脊的地下传来过可疑声音，各支点仍奉命坚守。电话与备用枪位分开安置，以免一次爆炸切断整壕联络。"),TEXT("Suspicious sounds have been heard beneath Messines Ridge. The strongpoints are still ordered to hold. Keep the telephone separate from reserve gun positions so one blast cannot sever the trench's communications."),TEXT("Suspicious sounds have been heard beneath Messines Ridge, yet every strongpoint is still ordered to hold. Separate the telephone from the reserve gun positions: one blast must not sever an entire trench's communications.")},
{TEXT("第二集团军已为梅西讷攻势准备数月，澳大利亚与新西兰部队也将参战。邻接部队送来坡面草图，标出弹坑、通路和枪位。"),TEXT("Second Army has prepared the Messines offensive for months, with Australian and New Zealand formations among its troops. A neighbouring unit sends a sketch marking crater rims, approaches and gun positions.")},
{TEXT("第二集团军已为梅西讷攻势准备数月，澳大利亚与新西兰部队也将参战。邻接部队送来坡面草图，标出弹坑、通路和枪位。"),TEXT("Second Army has prepared the Messines offensive for months, with Australian and New Zealand formations among its troops. A neighbouring unit sends a sketch marking crater rims, approaches and gun positions."),TEXT("第二集团军为梅西讷攻势做了漫长准备，澳大利亚与新西兰部队也在其中。邻接部队送来的坡面草图，比一张平直的箭头更能说明坑岸与枪位的关系。")},
{TEXT("第二集团军已为梅西讷攻势准备数月，澳大利亚与新西兰部队也将参战。邻接部队送来坡面草图，标出弹坑、通路和枪位。"),TEXT("Second Army has prepared the Messines offensive for months, with Australian and New Zealand formations among its troops. A neighbouring unit sends a sketch marking crater rims, approaches and gun positions."),TEXT("Second Army has prepared the Messines offensive for months, with Australian and New Zealand formations among its troops. A sketch of the slopes from a neighbouring unit says more about crater lips and gun positions than a straight arrow ever could.")},
{TEXT("邻段经验送达；可额外安排一次基础研习。"),TEXT("Notes from the neighbouring sector arrive. One additional course of basic training is available.")},
{TEXT("东线停火，西线未眠"),TEXT("The east falls silent; the west does not")},
{TEXT("联络线上的法军口音"),TEXT("French voices on the line")},
{TEXT("布列斯特和约让东线发生巨变，德国与奥匈帝国都面对新的调动。西线士兵听到的是增援将来的传言，看到的却仍是泥泞、弹药车和出发前的夜色。"),TEXT("Brest-Litovsk has transformed the Eastern Front. Germany and Austria-Hungary face new redeployments. In the west, soldiers hear rumours of reinforcements; before them lie the same mud, ammunition wagons and darkness before departure.")},
{TEXT("春季攻势撕开了旧有联络。英法两军需要重新接起彼此的边界；连队收到的是一张新的电话表，和邻段法军仍在坚守的消息。"),TEXT("The spring offensive has torn apart old liaison arrangements. British and French formations must reconnect their boundaries. The company receives a new telephone list, and word that the French next door are still holding.")},
{TEXT("前线战报送达连部，获得 1 研究点。"),TEXT("The front-line reports reach headquarters, awarding 1 research point.")},
{TEXT("前线战报送达连部，获得 1 研究点。"),TEXT("The front-line reports reach headquarters, awarding 1 research point."),TEXT("前线经验汇入连部；战绩点增加一。 ")},
{TEXT("前线战报送达连部，获得 1 研究点。"),TEXT("The front-line reports reach headquarters, awarding 1 research point."),TEXT("Front-line experience reaches company headquarters. One research point awarded. ")},
{TEXT("工兵走在前面"),TEXT("Pioneers go first")},
{TEXT("铁丝前的一把剪钳"),TEXT("Wire cutters at the obstacle")},
{TEXT("退却后的交通壕被旧铁丝、废弃弹药和临时障碍堵塞。工兵与喷火分队现已配属本连，反击时需要步兵和机枪掩护。"),TEXT("Old wire, abandoned ammunition and hasty obstacles block the communication trenches after the retreat. Pioneers and flame detachments are now attached to the company and need covering fire during the counterattack.")},
{TEXT("退却后的交通壕被旧铁丝、废弃弹药和临时障碍堵塞。工兵与喷火分队现已配属本连，反击时需要步兵和机枪掩护。"),TEXT("Old wire, abandoned ammunition and hasty obstacles block the communication trenches after the retreat. Pioneers and flame detachments are now attached to the company and need covering fire during the counterattack."),TEXT("退却没有让战场变得干净。旧铁丝、废弃弹药和临时障碍挡住自己的交通壕。工兵与喷火分队终于列入本连配属，短促反击必须给他们留下掩护。")},
{TEXT("退却后的交通壕被旧铁丝、废弃弹药和临时障碍堵塞。工兵与喷火分队现已配属本连，反击时需要步兵和机枪掩护。"),TEXT("Old wire, abandoned ammunition and hasty obstacles block the communication trenches after the retreat. Pioneers and flame detachments are now attached to the company and need covering fire during the counterattack."),TEXT("Retreat has not cleaned the battlefield. Old wire, abandoned ammunition and hasty obstacles obstruct your own communication trenches. Pioneers and flame detachments are finally available; short counterattacks must leave them covering fire.")},
{TEXT("推进中的连队又遇上了熟悉的障碍：铁丝、可疑引线和被炮火翻出的未爆弹。工兵开始随队。他们检查每一条引线，再让身后的步枪班通过。"),TEXT("The advancing company meets familiar obstacles: wire, suspect leads and unexploded shells turned up by the guns. Pioneers now accompany the column. They inspect each lead before letting the riflemen behind them pass.")},
{TEXT("工兵已可配属。出发前选择本次行动需要的分队与支援。"),TEXT("Pioneers are now available. Choose the sections and support needed for this operation before departure.")},
{TEXT("工兵已可配属。出发前选择本次行动需要的分队与支援。"),TEXT("Pioneers are now available. Choose the sections and support needed for this operation before departure."),TEXT("工兵配属；可用编制超出前线岗位时，出发前选择分队与支援。")},
{TEXT("工兵已可配属。出发前选择本次行动需要的分队与支援。"),TEXT("Pioneers are now available. Choose the sections and support needed for this operation before departure."),TEXT("Pioneers attached. When available formations exceed front-line positions, select sections and support before departure.")},
{TEXT("兴登堡防线的最后电话"),TEXT("The Hindenburg Line's last telephone")},
{TEXT("澳大利亚军团的接替令"),TEXT("Relief orders from the Australian Corps")},
{TEXT("运河隧道仍可容纳守军，地表交通壕却不断被截断。邻段请求援助，预备队须分批通过出口。"),TEXT("The canal tunnel still shelters defenders, but surface communication trenches are repeatedly cut. The neighbouring sector requests help; reserves must pass through the exits in separate groups.")},
{TEXT("运河隧道仍可容纳守军，地表交通壕却不断被截断。邻段请求援助，预备队须分批通过出口。"),TEXT("The canal tunnel still shelters defenders, but surface communication trenches are repeatedly cut. The neighbouring sector requests help; reserves must pass through the exits in separate groups."),TEXT("运河隧道仍可容纳守军，地表的交通壕却不断被截断。电话员把邻段的求援抄在纸上：不要让所有预备队挤在同一条出口里。")},
{TEXT("运河隧道仍可容纳守军，地表交通壕却不断被截断。邻段请求援助，预备队须分批通过出口。"),TEXT("The canal tunnel still shelters defenders, but surface communication trenches are repeatedly cut. The neighbouring sector requests help; reserves must pass through the exits in separate groups."),TEXT("The canal tunnel still shelters defenders, but surface communication trenches are repeatedly cut. A signaller copies the neighbouring sector's appeal onto paper: do not crowd every reserve into the same exit.")},
{TEXT("澳大利亚军团与配属的美军部队正在贝利库尔地段作战。法军喷火分遣队将支援你负责的邻接地段。工兵扩大突破口，让后续部队通过。"),TEXT("The Australian Corps and attached American troops are fighting around Bellicourt. A French flame detachment will support the neighbouring sector assigned to you. Pioneers must widen the breach for the following infantry.")},
{TEXT("纵深防御报告送达，获得 2 研究点。"),TEXT("Defence-in-depth reports arrive, awarding 2 research points.")},
{TEXT("纵深防御报告送达，获得 2 研究点。"),TEXT("Defence-in-depth reports arrive, awarding 2 research points."),TEXT("纵深防御经验送达；战绩点增加二。")},
{TEXT("纵深防御报告送达，获得 2 研究点。"),TEXT("Defence-in-depth reports arrive, awarding 2 research points."),TEXT("Defence-in-depth reports arrive. Two research points awarded.")},
{TEXT("接替战报送达，获得 2 研究点。法军 Schilt 分遣队现已可配属。"),TEXT("Relief reports arrive, awarding 2 research points. A French Schilt detachment is now available.")},
{TEXT("接替战报送达，获得 2 研究点。法军 Schilt 分遣队现已可配属。"),TEXT("Relief reports arrive, awarding 2 research points. A French Schilt detachment is now available."),TEXT("接替经验送达；战绩点增加二，法军 Schilt 分遣队可以配属。")},
{TEXT("接替战报送达，获得 2 研究点。法军 Schilt 分遣队现已可配属。"),TEXT("Relief reports arrive, awarding 2 research points. A French Schilt detachment is now available."),TEXT("Relief reports arrive. Two research points awarded; a French Schilt detachment is available.")},
{TEXT("留给铁路的最后一夜"),TEXT("One last night for the railway")},
{TEXT("休整令与河谷铁路"),TEXT("Relief orders and the valley railway")},
{TEXT("兴登堡防线已被突破，德军在塞勒河一带组织后卫。铁路运送物资并掩护撤离；装甲列车只能沿连通轨道行动，步兵须守住铁路通路。"),TEXT("The Hindenburg Line has been breached and German rearguards hold the Selle. The railway carries supplies and covers the evacuation. The armoured train needs connected track, with infantry guarding its approaches.")},
{TEXT("兴登堡防线已被突破，德军在塞勒河一带组织后卫。铁路运送物资并掩护撤离；装甲列车只能沿连通轨道行动，步兵须守住铁路通路。"),TEXT("The Hindenburg Line has been breached and German rearguards hold the Selle. The railway carries supplies and covers the evacuation. The armoured train needs connected track, with infantry guarding its approaches."),TEXT("兴登堡防线已被突破，塞勒河一带成为新的后卫阵地。铁路把撤运与火力绑在一起：装甲列车只能沿仍然连通的轨道行动，护路比盲目向前更重要。")},
{TEXT("兴登堡防线已被突破，德军在塞勒河一带组织后卫。铁路运送物资并掩护撤离；装甲列车只能沿连通轨道行动，步兵须守住铁路通路。"),TEXT("The Hindenburg Line has been breached and German rearguards hold the Selle. The railway carries supplies and covers the evacuation. The armoured train needs connected track, with infantry guarding its approaches."),TEXT("The Hindenburg Line has been breached. The Selle becomes a new rearguard position. Rail binds evacuation and firepower together: an armoured train can move only along connected track. Guarding the route matters more than a blind advance.")},
{TEXT("澳大利亚军团在十月初得到休整，其他部队继续渡过塞勒河。命令要求本连控制铁路切口。敌方装甲列车掩护着最后的撤运通路，炮兵必须先压住车上的枪口。"),TEXT("The Australian Corps is relieved in early October while other formations cross the Selle. Your company must secure the railway cutting. An enemy armoured train covers the last evacuation route; the artillery must first silence its guns.")},
{TEXT("装甲列车只在这段铁路行动出现；工兵与反装甲火力能改变通路争夺。"),TEXT("The armoured train appears only in this railway action. Pioneers and anti-armour fire can decide the struggle for the route.")},
{TEXT("南方停火的电报"),TEXT("A telegram from the southern front")},
{TEXT("城墙外的新西兰人"),TEXT("New Zealanders beneath the walls")},
{TEXT("奥匈帝国与协约国的停战协定开始生效，南方盟军的战争走到了尽头。西线仍在开火。连长收起电报，留下的命令只是带回还能归队的人。"),TEXT("The armistice between Austria-Hungary and the Allies takes effect. The southern ally's war is over, but the Western Front still fires. The captain folds the telegram. His remaining order is to bring back those who can still answer the roll.")},
{TEXT("新西兰部队正在勒凯努瓦一带作战，桑布尔河方向的推进也没有停止。平民尚未撤离，后卫仍在守住道路，残存障碍需要工兵清除。"),TEXT("New Zealand troops are fighting around Le Quesnoy, and the advance towards the Sambre continues. Civilians remain, rearguards hold the roads and pioneers must clear the remaining obstacles.")},
{TEXT("新西兰部队正在勒凯努瓦一带作战，桑布尔河方向的推进也没有停止。平民尚未撤离，后卫仍在守住道路，残存障碍需要工兵清除。"),TEXT("New Zealand troops are fighting around Le Quesnoy, and the advance towards the Sambre continues. Civilians remain, rearguards hold the roads and pioneers must clear the remaining obstacles."),TEXT("新西兰部队正在勒凯努瓦一带作战，桑布尔河方向的推进也没有停止。这里仍有平民、后卫和未拆除的障碍；胜利似乎已经临近，任何一发炮弹却都不会因此变轻。")},
{TEXT("新西兰部队正在勒凯努瓦一带作战，桑布尔河方向的推进也没有停止。平民尚未撤离，后卫仍在守住道路，残存障碍需要工兵清除。"),TEXT("New Zealand troops are fighting around Le Quesnoy, and the advance towards the Sambre continues. Civilians remain, rearguards hold the roads and pioneers must clear the remaining obstacles."),TEXT("New Zealand troops are fighting around Le Quesnoy, and the advance toward the Sambre has not stopped. Civilians, rearguards and uncleared obstacles remain. Victory may be close; no shell falls any more gently for it.")},
{TEXT("居民区附近禁用毒气与空中轰炸。地面火力掩护推进，工兵清除通路障碍。"),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited near civilians. Ground fire covers the advance while pioneers clear the approaches.")},
{TEXT("居民区附近禁用毒气与空中轰炸。地面火力掩护推进，工兵清除通路障碍。"),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited near civilians. Ground fire covers the advance while pioneers clear the approaches."),TEXT("居民区邻段限制毒气与空中轰炸；留下精确的地面掩护和工兵通路。")},
{TEXT("居民区附近禁用毒气与空中轰炸。地面火力掩护推进，工兵清除通路障碍。"),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited near civilians. Ground fire covers the advance while pioneers clear the approaches."),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are restricted near civilians. Retain precise ground support and a pioneer route.")},
{TEXT("在“%s”行动中配属后可研究。"),TEXT("Research available after assignment in “%s”.")},
{TEXT("在“%s”行动中配属后可研究。"),TEXT("Research available after assignment in “%s”."),TEXT("待「%s」的配属命令送达后研习。")},
{TEXT("在“%s”行动中配属后可研究。"),TEXT("Research available after assignment in “%s”."),TEXT("Await the attachment orders for %s before arranging this training.")},
{TEXT("尚未获得配属。"),TEXT("Not yet assigned.")},
{TEXT("尚未获得配属。"),TEXT("Not yet assigned."),TEXT("等待下一份配属命令。")},
{TEXT("尚未获得配属。"),TEXT("Not yet assigned."),TEXT("Awaiting the next attachment orders.")},
{TEXT("检查滤罐的封口"),TEXT("Check the filter seal")},
{TEXT("咬住口具，夹好鼻夹"),TEXT("Mouthpiece in; nose clip secure")},
{TEXT("防毒面具早已随军发放。工兵再教一遍气密检查，让滤罐远离泥水；警报响起时，完好的面罩能减少毒气造成的损失。"),TEXT("Respirator instruction begins with an airtight seal and a filter kept clear of muddy water. Once trained and equipped, the men can don their masks at the alarm and reduce losses to gas.")},
{TEXT("小盒式呼吸器需要练习正确佩戴口具与鼻夹，并定期检查软管和滤盒。防毒训练与完好的装备可减少毒气造成的损失。"),TEXT("Small-box respirator training covers the mouthpiece, nose clip, hose and filter box. Correct fitting and serviceable equipment reduce losses to gas.")},
{TEXT("小盒式呼吸器需要练习正确佩戴口具与鼻夹，并定期检查软管和滤盒。防毒训练与完好的装备可减少毒气造成的损失。"),TEXT("Small-box respirator training covers the mouthpiece, nose clip, hose and filter box. Correct fitting and serviceable equipment reduce losses to gas."),TEXT("不是今天才领到面具。小盒式呼吸器的口具与鼻夹必须用对，软管与滤盒也要检查；弄湿的滤材要更换，不能把保护自己的事留到警报响起以后。")},
{TEXT("小盒式呼吸器需要练习正确佩戴口具与鼻夹，并定期检查软管和滤盒。防毒训练与完好的装备可减少毒气造成的损失。"),TEXT("Small-box respirator training covers the mouthpiece, nose clip, hose and filter box. Correct fitting and serviceable equipment reduce losses to gas."),TEXT("The small-box respirator demands practice. Fit the mouthpiece and nose clip correctly; inspect the hose and filter box, and replace wet filter material. Arrange this equipment and training before the alarm sounds.")},
{TEXT("装备训练"),TEXT("Equipment training")},
{TEXT("装备训练"),TEXT("Equipment training"),TEXT("前沿装备")},
{TEXT("装备训练"),TEXT("Equipment training"),TEXT("Front-line equipment")},
{TEXT("探清每一条引线"),TEXT("Trace every lead")},
{TEXT("给后队留一条路"),TEXT("Leave a route for the next section")},
{TEXT("工兵练习在掩护下检查引线、标出可疑弹药，再剪开铁丝。通路开得更快，普通步兵却仍须等到他们完成工作。"),TEXT("Pioneers practise inspecting leads, marking suspect ammunition and cutting wire under covering fire. They open the route sooner, but ordinary infantry must still wait for the work to finish.")},
{TEXT("工兵通路"),TEXT("Pioneer routes")},
{TEXT("火焰后面的同伴"),TEXT("The men behind the flame")},
{TEXT("Schilt 分队的交接"),TEXT("The Schilt Detachment Arrives")},
{TEXT("Wex 喷火手的背后必须有人照看软管与燃料。整备好的储罐让短促喷射能够延续，步枪手仍要压住远处的枪口。"),TEXT("A Wex operator needs someone watching his hose and fuel supply. Prepared tanks sustain short bursts; riflemen must still silence the distant guns.")},
{TEXT("法军分遣队把喷火器的燃料与软管逐一交接。携行储备增加了，却没有让操作者免于枪弹；先掩护接近，再清理近处的掩体。"),TEXT("The French detachment hands over its fuel and hoses one by one. Extra reserves do not make the operator bulletproof. Cover the approach before clearing nearby shelters.")},
{TEXT("近壕清障"),TEXT("Clearing the Trench Approach")},
{TEXT("火墙向前挪动"),TEXT("Moving the Wall of Fire")},
{TEXT("跟在弹幕之后"),TEXT("Behind the Barrage")},
{TEXT("炮兵把落点逐段向前推移，在步兵面前留下短暂的低头时刻。核对新的火力表之后，徐进弹幕的每一步更紧密，少给敌人留下重新抬头的空隙。"),TEXT("The gunners move their fire forward in stages, keeping enemy heads down ahead of the infantry. A revised fire plan closes the gaps between each lift, leaving less time for the defenders to recover.")},
{TEXT("诸兵种联络"),TEXT("Combined Arms Liaison")},
{TEXT("双翼机的回报"),TEXT("A Report from the Biplane")},
{TEXT("地面铺开的信号布"),TEXT("Signal Panels on the Ground")},
{TEXT("联络机观察员通过地面信号报告敌情。训练后，报告维持更久，炮兵更早确认目标；地形和烟幕仍会妨碍观察。"),TEXT("The aircraft observer reports from ground signals. Training keeps reports useful for longer and helps the guns confirm targets sooner. Terrain and smoke still obstruct observation.")},
{TEXT("联络机观察员通过地面信号报告敌情。训练后，报告维持更久，炮兵更早确认目标；地形和烟幕仍会妨碍观察。"),TEXT("The aircraft observer reports from ground signals. Training keeps reports useful for longer and helps the guns confirm targets sooner. Terrain and smoke still obstruct observation."),TEXT("联络机飞过前沿，观察员辨认地面信号。报告能维持更久，也让炮兵更早确认目标；它既不能穿过山坡看人，也不会让步枪射穿烟雾。")},
{TEXT("联络机观察员通过地面信号报告敌情。训练后，报告维持更久，炮兵更早确认目标；地形和烟幕仍会妨碍观察。"),TEXT("The aircraft observer reports from ground signals. Training keeps reports useful for longer and helps the guns confirm targets sooner. Terrain and smoke still obstruct observation."),TEXT("A liaison aircraft crosses the front as its observer reads the ground panels. Reports remain useful longer and reach the guns sooner. They cannot reveal men behind a ridge or let rifles see through smoke.")},
{TEXT("红星升起就开炮"),TEXT("Fire When the Red Star Rises")},
{TEXT("预备好的 SOS 火线"),TEXT("A Prepared SOS Barrage")},
{TEXT("战线动摇，后方启封预备弹药。士气低落时，徐进弹幕、榴霰弹齐射与投弹任务获得优先补给，缩短再次整备的等待。"),TEXT("As the line falters, headquarters releases reserve ammunition. Low morale gives creeping barrages, shrapnel salvos and bombing missions priority for replenishment, shortening preparation for the next call.")},
{TEXT("别让轨道沉默"),TEXT("Keep the Rails Speaking")},
{TEXT("盯住铁轨的炮口"),TEXT("Guns Trained on the Railway")},
{TEXT("铁路炮组与前沿接起专线。列车仍被轨道限制，但炮位报告更清楚，后卫争取的片刻便能变成下一次掩护。"),TEXT("A dedicated line connects the railway gun crew to the front. The train remains bound to its rails, but clearer reports turn the rearguard's brief respite into another covering salvo.")},
{TEXT("观察员把列车炮位与铁路切口画在同一页上。专门的反装甲联络减少等待，逼迫那段移动的钢铁支点停止开火。"),TEXT("Observers mark the train's gun positions and the railway cutting on the same sheet. Dedicated anti-armour liaison shortens the wait to silence this moving strongpoint.")},
{TEXT("把老兵留在队伍里"),TEXT("Keep the Veterans in the Ranks")},
{TEXT("活下来的人带路"),TEXT("Let the Survivors Lead")},
{TEXT("让走过这些战场的老兵带领新来的补充兵。出发前的整备更快，不是因为他们不再害怕，而是每个人终于知道自己该站在哪里。"),TEXT("Veterans who know these battlefields guide the replacements. Preparations take less time because every man knows his place, even when he is afraid.")},
{TEXT("本次未配属喷火与工兵分队。"),TEXT("Flame troops and pioneers are not assigned to this operation.")},
{TEXT("本次未配属喷火与工兵分队。"),TEXT("Flame troops and pioneers are not assigned to this operation."),TEXT("此行动的命令尚未配属喷火与工兵分队。")},
{TEXT("本次未配属喷火与工兵分队。"),TEXT("Flame troops and pioneers are not assigned to this operation."),TEXT("Flamethrower and pioneer detachments have not been assigned to this operation.")},
{TEXT("守住中央通路，或击溃进攻部队"),TEXT("Hold the central approach or break the attacking force")},
{TEXT("夺取纵深阵地，或迫使守军停止抵抗"),TEXT("Take the positions in depth or force the defenders to give way")},
{TEXT("中央铁路支点连续驻守 175 秒；亦可击溃敌军"),TEXT("Hold the central railway position for 175 seconds, or break the enemy")},
{TEXT("中央通路连续驻守 155 秒；亦可击溃敌军"),TEXT("Hold the central approach for 155 seconds, or break the enemy")},
{TEXT("斯卡尔普：铁丝后的后卫"),TEXT("Scarpe: The Rearguard Behind the Wire")},
{TEXT("越过白垩田野"),TEXT("Across the Chalk Fields")},
{TEXT("法国 · 斯卡尔普河战区"),TEXT("France · Scarpe Sector")},
{TEXT("亚眠之后，协约军继续扩大攻势。斯卡尔普河方向的推进越过旧阵地与白垩农田；德国后卫利用尚存的铁丝、村落与交通壕争取时间。"),TEXT("After Amiens, the Allies press their advantage. The advance towards the Scarpe crosses old positions and chalk farmland; German rearguards use surviving wire, villages and communication trenches to buy time.")},
{TEXT("别把工兵当作另一支步枪班。先清理自己需要的通路，再让喷火手借烟幕靠近失守的壕角；机枪要给后卫留下退路。"),TEXT("Pioneers are more than another rifle section. Clear the route you need, then let the flamethrowers approach a lost trench corner behind smoke. Keep the machineguns covering a way out.")},
{TEXT("工兵检查铁丝与可疑弹药，步枪留在能掩护他们的位置。为本次出击选择五支分队的编制，给徐进弹幕保留一条联络。"),TEXT("Pioneers inspect the wire and suspicious ammunition while riflemen cover them. Select five detachments for this operation and keep a liaison channel open for the creeping barrage.")},
{TEXT("白垩土的壕肩呈浅灰断面，铁丝沿田界分布；可疑地段有通路，分散前进比挤在一起更安全。"),TEXT("Pale chalk shows along the trench shoulders, with wire following the field boundaries. Routes remain through suspicious ground; a dispersed advance is safer than a crowded one.")},
{TEXT("运河下面仍有人"),TEXT("Men Beneath the Canal")},
{TEXT("贝利库尔的地表"),TEXT("Above Bellicourt")},
{TEXT("法国 · 圣康坦运河"),TEXT("France · St Quentin Canal")},
{TEXT("圣康坦运河是兴登堡防线的重要障碍。澳大利亚与美军在贝利库尔隧道上方作战，英国部队在其他渡口推进；攻势仍需突破后方的纵深阵地。"),TEXT("The St Quentin Canal is a major obstacle in the Hindenburg Line. Australian and American troops fight above the Bellicourt tunnel while British units advance at other crossings. Further defensive positions await beyond the crossing.")},
{TEXT("圣康坦运河是兴登堡防线的重要障碍。澳大利亚与美军在贝利库尔隧道上方作战，英国部队在其他渡口推进；攻势仍需突破后方的纵深阵地。"),TEXT("The St Quentin Canal is a major obstacle in the Hindenburg Line. Australian and American troops fight above the Bellicourt tunnel while British units advance at other crossings. Further defensive positions await beyond the crossing."),TEXT("圣康坦运河构成兴登堡防线的重要障碍。澳大利亚与美军在贝利库尔隧道上方作战，英国部队也在其他渡口推进；纵深防御让突破远非一条直线。")},
{TEXT("圣康坦运河是兴登堡防线的重要障碍。澳大利亚与美军在贝利库尔隧道上方作战，英国部队在其他渡口推进；攻势仍需突破后方的纵深阵地。"),TEXT("The St Quentin Canal is a major obstacle in the Hindenburg Line. Australian and American troops fight above the Bellicourt tunnel while British units advance at other crossings. Further defensive positions await beyond the crossing."),TEXT("The St Quentin Canal forms a major obstacle in the Hindenburg Line. Australian and American troops fight above the Bellicourt tunnel while British units advance at other crossings. Defence in depth makes the breakthrough anything but a straight march.")},
{TEXT("把枪位藏在错开的壕肩之后。工兵维持交通，喷火队留在近处反击；不要把守军全部塞进隧道上方的狭小地带。"),TEXT("Hide gun positions behind staggered trench shoulders. Pioneers keep communications open; flamethrowers wait close by for counterattacks. Do not crowd the garrison into the narrow ground above the tunnel.")},
{TEXT("用工兵打开壕前障碍，再让法军 Schilt 分遣队清理近处掩体。澳美主攻在邻段，联络官要求本连控制隧道两侧的接近线。地表旧壕与地下通道交错，逐段查明敌军位置再推进。"),TEXT("Pioneers open the obstacles before the French Schilt detachment clears nearby shelters. Australian and American troops lead the assault next door; this company must control the tunnel approaches. Locate the defenders among the old trenches and underground passages before advancing.")},
{TEXT("深切运河与草坡、之字壕和密集铁丝交错。爆破障碍与弹坑挤压通路，烟幕应覆盖整段渡口。"),TEXT("A deep canal cutting, grassy slopes, zigzag trenches and dense wire divide the field. Demolished obstacles and craters constrict the approaches. Smoke should cover the whole crossing.")},
{TEXT("塞勒河：争夺铁路"),TEXT("The Selle: contest the railway")},
{TEXT("塞勒河：争夺铁路"),TEXT("The Selle: contest the railway"),TEXT("塞勒河：留住铁轨")},
{TEXT("塞勒河：争夺铁路"),TEXT("The Selle: contest the railway"),TEXT("The Selle: Hold the Railway")},
{TEXT("铁路切口"),TEXT("The railway cutting")},
{TEXT("铁路切口"),TEXT("The railway cutting"),TEXT("切口里的钢铁")},
{TEXT("铁路切口"),TEXT("The railway cutting"),TEXT("Steel in the Cutting")},
{TEXT("法国 · 塞勒河谷"),TEXT("France · Selle Valley")},
{TEXT("塞勒河战役中，英军与相邻法军继续向东推进，德军依靠河谷、铁路与村落组织后卫。后卫依靠沿河铁路输送弹药、撤离装备，列车火力正在掩护守军保住最后的通路。"),TEXT("British and neighbouring French forces continue east during the Battle of the Selle. German rearguards draw on the river valley, railway and villages. Trains bring ammunition and remove equipment while railway guns cover the last open routes.")},
{TEXT("列车需要可通行的铁轨，步兵需要列车压住远处枪口。守住中央切口，派工兵清理接近通路，把迫击炮留给靠近铁轨的敌人。"),TEXT("The train needs clear rails; the infantry need its guns to keep distant weapons quiet. Secure the central cutting, use pioneers to clear the approaches and reserve mortars for troops closing on the track.")},
{TEXT("敌方装甲列车沿河谷铁路活动。工兵先检查接近线，反装甲炮盯住炮车；利用烟幕轮换夺取切口，别让所有人都暴露在铁轨旁。"),TEXT("An enemy armoured train patrols the valley railway. Pioneers inspect the approaches while anti-armour guns watch its gun car. Use smoke to rotate troops through the cutting instead of exposing everyone beside the rails.")},
{TEXT("铁路越过湿润河谷，路堤提供局部遮蔽。轨道旁散布障碍与废弃物，纵向展开的通路更宽。"),TEXT("The railway crosses a wet river valley, its embankment offering patches of cover. Obstacles and debris lie beside the track, with broader routes along the valley.")},
{TEXT("桑布尔：最后的后卫"),TEXT("The Sambre: The Last Rearguard")},
{TEXT("停战以前的清晨"),TEXT("Dawn Before the Armistice")},
{TEXT("法国 · 桑布尔与勒凯努瓦战区"),TEXT("France · Sambre and Le Quesnoy Sector")},
{TEXT("桑布尔方向的攻势展开，新西兰部队在勒凯努瓦作战。奥匈帝国的停战已经生效，西线尚未停火；后卫阵地、运河与仍有居民的村镇继续阻挡前进。"),TEXT("The Sambre offensive opens as New Zealand troops fight at Le Quesnoy. Austria-Hungary's armistice has taken effect, but the Western Front still fires. Rearguard positions, canals and inhabited villages continue to bar the way.")},
{TEXT("不要把最后的交通壕变成死胡同。工兵保持出口，机枪交替掩护；居民区邻段不批准毒气与空中轰炸，靠仍能互相支援的小队守住通路。"),TEXT("Do not let the last communication trench become a dead end. Pioneers keep exits clear while machineguns cover in turn. Gas and bombing are forbidden near the inhabited sector; hold the routes with sections that can support one another.")},
{TEXT("在村落边缘保持克制的火力，工兵先行。新西兰人在邻段城墙外作战，本连要控制通路；毒气和空中轰炸均不列入本次命令。"),TEXT("Use restrained fire along the village edge and let the pioneers lead. New Zealand troops are fighting by the neighbouring town walls; this company must control the approaches. Gas and aerial bombing are not authorised for this operation.")},
{TEXT("破墙、果树与草沟分割射界，斜向交通壕通往运河。零散铁丝与可疑障碍仍能夺走生命。"),TEXT("Broken walls, orchards and grassy ditches divide the fields of fire. Angled communication trenches lead towards the canal. Scattered wire and suspicious obstacles remain deadly.")},
{TEXT("本次在城郊作战，禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are unavailable for this operation near town.")},
{TEXT("本次在城郊作战，禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are unavailable for this operation near town."),TEXT("本次命令不批准居民区邻段的毒气与空中轰炸。")},
{TEXT("本次在城郊作战，禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are unavailable for this operation near town."),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are not authorised beside the inhabited sector.")},
{TEXT("工兵与 Wex 分队归建。"),TEXT("Pioneer and Wex detachments have rejoined the command.")},
{TEXT("工兵配属，新的支援联络需要出发前安排。"),TEXT("Pioneers are assigned. Arrange the new support liaison before departure.")},
{TEXT("法军 Schilt 分遣队将在圣康坦运河行动加入。"),TEXT("A French Schilt detachment will join the St Quentin Canal operation.")},
{TEXT("纵深守军仍与邻段保持联络。"),TEXT("Defenders in depth remain in contact with neighbouring sectors.")},
{TEXT("澳美部队在邻段作战，法军 Schilt 分遣队可配属本连。"),TEXT("Australian and American troops fight in the neighbouring sector. The French Schilt detachment can be assigned to this company.")},
{TEXT("澳美部队在邻段作战，法军 Schilt 分遣队可配属本连。"),TEXT("Australian and American troops fight in the neighbouring sector. The French Schilt detachment can be assigned to this company."),TEXT("邻段澳美军团作战；本连可接纳法军 Schilt 分遣队。")},
{TEXT("澳美部队在邻段作战，法军 Schilt 分遣队可配属本连。"),TEXT("Australian and American troops fight in the neighbouring sector. The French Schilt detachment can be assigned to this company."),TEXT("Australian and American corps fight next door; a French Schilt detachment is available to this company.")},
{TEXT("铁路后卫正在掩护撤运，装甲列车支援本段。"),TEXT("The railway rearguard covers the evacuation. An armoured train supports this sector.")},
{TEXT("澳大利亚军团休整，英法军队继续推进。"),TEXT("The Australian Corps rests while British and French forces continue the advance.")},
{TEXT("奥匈帝国停战的消息已经传来。"),TEXT("News has arrived of Austria-Hungary's armistice.")},
{TEXT("新西兰部队正在勒凯努瓦方向作战。"),TEXT("New Zealand troops are fighting towards Le Quesnoy.")},
{TEXT(" · 选择覆盖地段"),TEXT(" · Select the area to cover")},
{TEXT("鼠标右键取消"),TEXT("Right-click to cancel")},
{TEXT("新兵种随战役进程开放"),TEXT("New formations become available as the campaign progresses")},
{TEXT("新兵种随战役进程开放"),TEXT("New formations become available as the campaign progresses"),TEXT("随战役推进获得新的配属")},
{TEXT("新兵种随战役进程开放"),TEXT("New formations become available as the campaign progresses"),TEXT("Further attachments become available as the campaign advances")},
{TEXT("快捷键  %d"),TEXT("Shortcut  %d")},
{TEXT("预计 %.0f–%.0f 秒后抵达\n%s"),TEXT("Arrival expected in %.0f–%.0f seconds\n%s")},
{TEXT("快捷键  "),TEXT("Shortcut  ")},
{TEXT("设置 · O"),TEXT("Settings · O")},
{TEXT("作战手册 · H"),TEXT("Field Manual · H")},
{TEXT("中央驻守进度  %.0f%%"),TEXT("Hold progress  %.0f%%")},
{TEXT("中央驻守进度  %.0f%%"),TEXT("Hold progress  %.0f%%"),TEXT("守住中央阵地  %.0f%%")},
{TEXT("中央驻守进度  %.0f%%"),TEXT("Hold progress  %.0f%%"),TEXT("Hold the central position  %.0f%%")},
{TEXT("已接令"),TEXT("Order acknowledged")},
{TEXT("已接令"),TEXT("Order acknowledged"),TEXT("已受理")},
{TEXT("已接令"),TEXT("Order acknowledged"),TEXT("Acknowledged")},
{TEXT("命令已传往后方"),TEXT("Orders relayed to the rear")},
{TEXT("占领"),TEXT("Captured")},
{TEXT("失守"),TEXT("Position lost")},
{TEXT("误伤"),TEXT("Friendly fire")},
{TEXT("烟幕"),TEXT("Smoke Screen")},
{TEXT("烟幕已接令"),TEXT("Smoke mission acknowledged")},
{TEXT("烟幕已接令"),TEXT("Smoke mission acknowledged"),TEXT("烟幕任务已受理")},
{TEXT("火力任务已下达"),TEXT("Fire mission acknowledged")},
{TEXT("火力任务已下达"),TEXT("Fire mission acknowledged"),TEXT("火力任务已受理")},
{TEXT("埃德蒙·艾伦比"),TEXT("Edmund Allenby")},
{TEXT("英军第三集团军 · 阿拉斯，1917"),TEXT("British Third Army · Arras, 1917")},
{TEXT("骑兵军官出身，1915年起统率第三集团军。阿拉斯攻势中，他试图以密集炮火打开斯卡普河谷；雪幕下的突进很快又受到德军阵地与补给距离的牵制。"),TEXT("A cavalry officer who commanded Third Army from 1915. At Arras he sought to open the Scarpe valley with concentrated artillery. The advance through snow soon met the limits imposed by German positions and lengthening supply routes.")},
{TEXT("赫伯特·普卢默"),TEXT("Herbert Plumer")},
{TEXT("英军第二集团军 · 梅西讷，1917"),TEXT("British Second Army · Messines, 1917")},
{TEXT("一位重视周密准备的集团军司令。梅西讷的地道、炮兵与步兵计划在他麾下合为一体：先夺山脊，再稳固阵地，让反击撞上已经转向的炮口。"),TEXT("An army commander known for thorough preparation. At Messines he brought mining, artillery and infantry plans together: take the ridge, consolidate, then meet the counterattack with guns already trained on its approach.")},
{TEXT("休伯特·高夫"),TEXT("Hubert Gough")},
{TEXT("英军第五集团军 · 伊普尔与圣康坦"),TEXT("British Fifth Army · Ypres and St Quentin")},
{TEXT("1917年，他指挥第五集团军向皮尔肯山脊进攻；1918年春，同一支部队又被拉到漫长的圣康坦正面。从追求突破到掩护撤退，他的战绩始终伴随着激烈争议。"),TEXT("He led Fifth Army towards Pilckem Ridge in 1917. In spring 1918 the same army held an extended front around St Quentin. From seeking a breakthrough to covering a retreat, his record remained fiercely disputed.")},
{TEXT("朱利安·宾"),TEXT("Julian Byng")},
{TEXT("英军第三集团军 · 康布雷，1917"),TEXT("British Third Army · Cambrai, 1917")},
{TEXT("曾率加拿大军攻取维米岭，随后接掌第三集团军。康布雷的坦克、步兵与炮火协同显示了新的突破可能；十天后的德军反击，也暴露了突出部难以巩固的代价。"),TEXT("After commanding the Canadian Corps at Vimy Ridge, he took over Third Army. Cambrai showed the promise of tanks, infantry and artillery working together. The German counterattack ten days later exposed the cost of holding a vulnerable salient.")},
{TEXT("亨利·罗林森"),TEXT("Henry Rawlinson")},
{TEXT("英军第四集团军 · 亚眠，1918"),TEXT("British Fourth Army · Amiens, 1918")},
{TEXT("1918年8月，他在亚眠组织第四集团军的突击。英国第三军与澳大利亚、加拿大两军分据索姆河两侧，在隐蔽集结与炮坦协同下展开攻势；法国第一集团军在南翼并肩作战。"),TEXT("He organised Fourth Army's attack at Amiens in August 1918. British III Corps and the Australian and Canadian corps advanced on either side of the Somme after concealed preparations, with coordinated guns and tanks. French First Army fought on the southern flank.")},
{TEXT("路德维希·冯·法尔肯豪森"),TEXT("Ludwig von Falkenhausen")},
{TEXT("德军第六集团军 · 阿拉斯，1917"),TEXT("German Sixth Army · Arras, 1917")},
{TEXT("经历过普奥、普法战争的普鲁士老将。1917年4月，他统率第六集团军面对阿拉斯攻势。阵地与预备队未能及时止住英军最初的突入，他在当月离开前线指挥岗位。"),TEXT("A Prussian veteran of the Austro-Prussian and Franco-Prussian wars. Sixth Army faced the Arras offensive under his command in April 1917. Its positions and reserves failed to halt the initial British advance; he left his front-line command that month.")},
{TEXT("弗里德里希·西克斯特·冯·阿尔明"),TEXT("Friedrich Sixt von Armin")},
{TEXT("德军第四集团军 · 佛兰德，1917"),TEXT("German Fourth Army · Flanders, 1917")},
{TEXT("1917年指挥第四集团军守卫佛兰德。从梅西讷山脊到伊普尔突出部，他的部队依托混凝土据点、纵深阵地与反击部队抵挡协约国攻势，也承受了矿坑与泥海中的惨重消耗。"),TEXT("He commanded Fourth Army in Flanders in 1917. From Messines Ridge to the Ypres salient, his troops relied on concrete strongpoints, defence in depth and counterattacks, enduring severe losses among the mine craters and mud.")},
{TEXT("格奥尔格·冯·德·马维茨"),TEXT("Georg von der Marwitz")},
{TEXT("德军第二集团军 · 康布雷至亚眠"),TEXT("German Second Army · Cambrai to Amiens")},
{TEXT("第二集团军司令。1917年康布雷反击、1918年春的迈克尔攻势，都有他麾下部队的身影；到了亚眠，这支军队转而面对协约国的炮兵、坦克和步兵协同突击。"),TEXT("Commander of Second Army. His formations fought in the Cambrai counterattack of 1917 and Operation Michael in spring 1918. At Amiens they instead faced an Allied assault combining artillery, tanks and infantry.")},
{TEXT("亨利·霍恩"),TEXT("Henry Horne")},
{TEXT("英军第一集团军 · 斯卡尔普，1918"),TEXT("British First Army · Scarpe, 1918")},
{TEXT("第一集团军司令。八月二十六日，他的部队以加拿大军为先导，在斯卡尔普河与桑塞河掩护的翼侧向东推进。眼前的任务是越过旧阵地，让炮兵与补给跟上持续变化的战线。"),TEXT("Commander of First Army. On 26 August his troops advanced east with the Canadian Corps in the lead and their flanks protected by the Scarpe and Sensee rivers. The task was to cross old positions while bringing guns and supplies up behind the moving front.")},
{TEXT("英军第四集团军 · 圣康坦运河，1918"),TEXT("British Fourth Army · St Quentin Canal, 1918")},
{TEXT("第四集团军由亚眠继续向兴登堡防线推进。澳大利亚与配属美军在贝利库尔作战，其他渡口同样需要炮火、步兵与工兵配合；运河的深切地形让每一条通路都至关重要。"),TEXT("Fourth Army advanced from Amiens towards the Hindenburg Line. Australian and attached American troops fought at Bellicourt, while other crossings also demanded close cooperation between gunners, infantry and pioneers. The deep canal cutting made every approach vital.")},
{TEXT("英军第四集团军 · 塞勒河，1918"),TEXT("British Fourth Army · Selle, 1918")},
{TEXT("突破兴登堡防线之后，第四集团军继续追击到塞勒河。曾经依托连续战壕的战争再次转入河谷与村落，桥头、道路和邻军联络决定了推进能否持续。"),TEXT("After breaking the Hindenburg Line, Fourth Army pursued the enemy to the Selle. The war moved from continuous trench systems into valleys and villages. Bridgeheads, roads and contact with neighbouring formations determined whether the advance could continue.")},
{TEXT("英军第三集团军 · 桑布尔北翼，1918"),TEXT("British Third Army · Northern Sambre Sector, 1918")},
{TEXT("第三集团军在百日攻势中继续向东推进，新西兰师也在其序列内。勒凯努瓦的城墙与桑布尔战区的村落仍有守军；停战以前的最后一周，前线的任务并没有因胜利将近而变得轻松。"),TEXT("Third Army continued east during the Hundred Days, with the New Zealand Division among its formations. Le Quesnoy's walls and the Sambre villages still held defenders. The last week before the armistice brought no easy duty at the front.")},
{TEXT("奥托·冯·贝洛"),TEXT("Otto von Below")},
{TEXT("德军第十七集团军 · 斯卡尔普，1918"),TEXT("German Seventeenth Army · Scarpe, 1918")},
{TEXT("先后经历东线、马其顿和意大利战场，二月起接掌第十七集团军。春季的进攻已转为夏末的防御，他的部队需要用旧阵地和后卫争取时间，抵挡斯卡尔普方向的持续压力。"),TEXT("After service on the Eastern, Macedonian and Italian fronts, he took command of Seventeenth Army in February. Spring's offensive had become late summer's defence. Old positions and rearguards had to buy time against sustained pressure along the Scarpe.")},
{TEXT("阿道夫·冯·卡洛维茨"),TEXT("Adolph von Carlowitz")},
{TEXT("德军第二集团军 · 圣康坦运河，1918"),TEXT("German Second Army · St Quentin Canal, 1918")},
{TEXT("萨克森军人，曾任王国战争大臣并指挥军级部队。九月下旬接掌第二集团军时，兴登堡防线正面临协约军的新一轮攻势；他的职责是让分散的支点继续构成能够互相支援的防御。"),TEXT("A Saxon officer, former war minister and corps commander. When he took over Second Army in late September, the Hindenburg Line faced another Allied offensive. His task was to keep scattered strongpoints fighting as a mutually supporting defence.")},
{TEXT("德军第二集团军 · 塞勒河，1918"),TEXT("German Second Army · Selle, 1918")},
{TEXT("第二集团军在持续后撤中寻找新的立足点。河流和铁路可以帮助后卫争取时间，却无法替代步兵守住通路；从纵深防线到河谷阵地，保存联络已和保存兵力同样困难。"),TEXT("Second Army sought fresh footholds during its continuing retreat. Rivers and railways could buy the rearguards time but could not replace infantry on the approaches. Maintaining communications was becoming as difficult as preserving manpower.")},
{TEXT("布鲁诺·冯·穆德拉"),TEXT("Bruno von Mudra")},
{TEXT("德军第十七集团军 · 桑布尔北翼，1918"),TEXT("German Seventeenth Army · Northern Sambre Sector, 1918")},
{TEXT("工兵出身，长期从事工程兵与要塞事务，曾在阿尔贡指挥作战。十月十二日接掌第十七集团军之后，他面对的是不断后移的战线；河岸、村落与有限的交通线成为最后的后卫依托。"),TEXT("An engineer officer with long experience of fortifications and earlier command in the Argonne. After taking over Seventeenth Army on 12 October, he faced a steadily receding front. Riverbanks, villages and limited roads became the last rearguard positions.")},
